# tutor-core reads no environment variables, and should not.
#
# This is the pure domain and application package: no I/O, no frameworks, no
# configuration. import-linter enforces it — the "Domain imports no
# frameworks" contract forbids sqlalchemy, psycopg, fastapi, httpx and the
# rest — and a settings object here would be the first step back across that
# line. What the domain needs is handed to it through an injected port
# (DEC-0001); it never reads a value for itself.
#
# Configuration belongs to the adapters that perform the I/O. See
# tutor-api/.env.example.
#
# The file exists so the absence reads as a decision rather than an oversight.
# If something here ever appears to need an environment variable, that is a
# sign the logic belongs in an adapter, not that this file should gain a line.
